<div class="prose">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <span class="updated">Last updated July 2026</span>

  <p>
    This policy explains what Repverse collects, why, and how it's used. Repverse is built to work
    with public blockchain data — most of what you see when you look up a wallet is not personal
    data at all, it's data that already exists on the Stacks blockchain.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account info:</strong> if you sign in with Google, we store your name, email, and profile photo. If you connect a wallet, we store your public STX address.</li>
    <li><strong>Watchlist data:</strong> wallets or BNS names you choose to save for quick access.</li>
    <li><strong>Lookup history:</strong> anonymized search queries, used to improve caching and show recently searched wallets.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
  <p>
    Repverse never asks for or stores your private keys, seed phrases, or wallet passwords. Wallet
    connection only shares your public address, the same information visible to anyone viewing a
    transaction on-chain.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use data</h2>
  <p>
    Account and watchlist data is used only to power features like saved wallets and personalized
    dashboards. We don't sell personal data to third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Repverse queries the Stacks blockchain API for chain data and the CoinMarketCap API for currency
    conversion rates. These requests may be logged by those providers according to their own
    privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your account and associated watchlist at any time from your dashboard, or by
    contacting us. Disconnecting your wallet or signing out of Google ends your session immediately.
  </p>
</div>
